Fix false positive ``invalid-name`` for ``TypeAlias``, ``TypeVar``, ``ParamSpec`` and
``TypeVarTuple`` defined in a class body: they are now checked against their own
naming style instead of ``class-attribute-naming-style``.

With the default configuration this can also add new ``invalid-name`` messages:
``class-attribute-naming-style`` defaults to ``any``, so class-body names such as
``t = TypeVar("t")`` or ``alias: TypeAlias = int`` were not checked before.

Closes #11809
